  {"title": "U5 - PuLID (SDXL v1.1) identity with COMPOSITIONAL FREEDOM. Same prompt, seed, steps and cfg as the E14b InstantID run, so the two are directly comparable. RESULT: InstantID returned a bust (face = 33.0% of frame, cos 0.823); PuLID returned the full-body path scene the prompt asked for (face = 9.8% of frame, cos 0.313). Both sit far above the prompt-level baseline (0.143). So the two are NOT ranked - they are different jobs: InstantID for tight identity portraits, PuLID for identity inside a free composition. method='fidelity' favours resemblance, 'style' frees the checkpoint; ApplyPulidAdvanced adds a fidelity slider and projection. Needs facexlib + insightface/antelopev2 + EVA-CLIP (auto-downloaded) + cubiq/PuLID_ComfyUI + ip-adapter_pulid_sdxl_fp16.safetensors. Use a SHARP reference - the EVA-CLIP path is sensitive to reference quality.", "bounding": [-1240, -180, 2500, 1000], "color": "#6b3f9e", "font_size": 22, "flags": {}}
